# What never belongs in the build context.
#
# There was no such file until the image started building the viewer, and that
# is what made one necessary: the site stage copies web/ wholesale, and without
# these lines it would copy web/node_modules and a web/dist left behind by a
# local `npm run build` -- the second of which would then shadow the fresh
# build with whatever happened to be on the machine.
#
# Everything here is either generated or irrelevant to a server image. The Go
# stage copies three named paths and is unaffected; this only shrinks what has
# to be sent to the daemon before it starts.

**/node_modules
web/dist
frontend/dist
frontend/bindings

bin
.task
.tmp-verify
build/linux/appimage/build

.git
.github
.claude
